\subtree{
\title{5.3 Correctness}

\ol{
\li{\strong{\code{\verb~|evc~} alone is counter-identical to v0} (section 5.2): six counters equal on three corpora, which a cell that returned anything but what \code{\verb~|VAL~} holds would have to leave untouched.}
\li{\strong{The machine's verdicts are the same in every row of section 5.2}: accepted, rejected and declined counts of the machine are equal with the switch off and on (Cedar slice 8,053 / 0 / 22, Init 57,774 / 0 / 328, reachability 4,216 / 0 / 16, Std 99,893 / 0 / 406, con-leche 36,186 / 0 / 176), and the statistics \code{\verb~|driver.declined~} and \code{\verb~|driver.machineIncomplete~} are 0 in every run.}
\li{\p{\strong{Per declaration against the reference engine} (M8's differential harness, \code{\verb~|rlvm.machine.M8Main diff~}, run on the sandbox tree with the reports under a private root, \code{\verb~|work/prof/X1/diff.sh~}; reports: \code{\verb~|work/prof/X1/root~\verb~|/work/status/machine-diff-*.txt~}). \code{\verb~|base~} is the sandbox with the switch off; \code{\verb~|evc-once~} = \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.m2.x=640~}, \code{\verb~|once~} = 128, \code{\verb~|evc-once-prof~} = 896; \code{\verb~|s1-~} = with \code{\verb~|-Dm8.switches=warm,gated,expect~}.}
