\p{Every "machine declined" in these reports is the base tree's own decline of declarations that enter eager reduction (M6's \code{\verb~|erDeclines~} of 15:07Z; with the switch off the same test declines: rows \code{\verb~|*-base~}, and on the corpora the machine's declined counts are equal off and on, section 5.2); the reference engine checked them. No report has a SOUNDNESS or COMPLETENESS line, a crash or a timeout. Rows \code{\verb~|*-rebased-*~} are the full prototype on the main tree of 16:12Z (\code{\verb~|work/prof/X1/rebased/~}), rows \code{\verb~|*-onceonly-*~} the GO patch on the main tree of 16:53Z (item 4), the others the sandbox tree as measured. A run over all 230 published tests with \code{\verb~|evc + once~} was started and stopped by me after 15 minutes in the heavy perf files; it wrote no report and is no evidence. That the harness really ran with the switches shows in its tick counts: tutorial 6,916 ticks with the switch off, 6,917 with \code{\verb~|evc + once~}, 7,222 with \code{\verb~|once~} alone, 5,924 under s1 with \code{\verb~|evc + once~}; bugs 166,853 / 166,931 / 175,178 / 105,282.}}
\li{\strong{The GO patch on the moving main tree.} \code{\verb~|0001~} is \code{\verb~|once~} alone on the main tree as copied at 16:53:19Z (\code{\verb~|work/prof/X1/once-only/~}). In the harness (which sets the switches itself: none) it gives the tick counts of the measured build with \code{\verb~|once~} (tutorial 7,222; reachability 34,824,170 against 34,824,165 through the launcher) and the rows \code{\verb~|*-onceonly-once~} above: tutorial clean, bugs 1,427 / 1,428, the Cedar slice 8,407 / 8,418, reachability 4,405 / 4,413, no SOUNDNESS, no COMPLETENESS. Through the launcher that tree no longer runs v0 when no switch is given: its provider now defaults to \code{\verb~|gated,expect,warm~} with a 1 MiB cap (statistics: \code{\verb~|machine.switches~}, \code{\verb~|sessionCapBytes~}). Against that default, with the filter (\code{\verb~|work/prof/X1/ab/counters-rebased.tsv~}): Cedar slice ticks 16.55 M -> 17.42 M (+5.3 \%), records 8.31 M -> 7.02 M (-15.6 \%), run words -11.4 \%; reachability ticks 35.53 M -> 35.68 M (+0.4 \%), records 20.74 M -> 12.93 M (-37.6 \%), run words -39.4 \%; accepted / declined unchanged (8,053 / 22 and 4,216 / 16). The module's fast test group on that tree, switch off: 412 tests, 0 failures, 3 skipped (\code{\verb~|work/prof/X1/once-only/fast-tests.out~}). No timing was taken on that tree.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{5.4 Time}

\p{Through \src{bench/quiet.py} only (one measurement at a time on the host, the 8 performance cores reserved): five windows between 16:35Z and 17:14Z (95 s, 112 s, 103 s, 71 s, 154 s). One JVM per row and round (launcher flags, SerialGC, C2, \code{\verb~|-Xms6g -Xmx6g -Xmn1g~}, one worker, statistics off), the export checked several times in the same process (\code{\verb~|-X passes=N -X passes-mode=recheck~}: pass 1 loads and checks cold, every later pass checks the loaded store again with new engine instances; N = 3 on the Cedar slice, 2 on reachability and Init); the configurations of a window interleaved. "check ms" is the driver's wall clock of the checking phase of a pass. The JVMs ran the sandbox jar (the measured build) next to the driver / main jars published at 16:02Z (the ones that know \code{\verb~|passes~}); with those jars v0 and s1 are the same configurations as in section 5.2 (session cap 4 MiB under s1). Raw lines and the tables per window: \code{\verb~|work/prof/X1/timing/passes.tsv~}, \code{\verb~|passes-extra.tsv~}, \code{\verb~|passes.md~}, \code{\verb~|passes-extra.md~}.}

\table{
\tr{\th{corpus}\th{configuration}\th{processes}\th{pass 1 check ms (cold), mean}\th{LAST pass check ms, every process}\th{mean}\th{range}\th{mean against v0 (s1 rows: against s1)}\th{ranges disjoint from the base row's}\th{verdicts}}
\tr{\td{reachability}\td{v0}\td{2}\td{6816}\td{5688 5686}\td{5687}\td{5686 - 5688}\td{-}\td{-}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{reachability}\td{v0 + once}\td{2}\td{5246}\td{4204 4082}\td{4143}\td{4082 - 4204}\td{-27.1\%}\td{yes}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{reachability}\td{v0 + evc + once}\td{2}\td{5539}\td{4451 4392}\td{4422}\td{4392 - 4451}\td{-22.3\%}\td{yes}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{reachability}\td{s1}\td{4}\td{6686}\td{5861 5454 5756 5270}\td{5585}\td{5270 - 5861}\td{-}\td{-}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{reachability}\td{s1 + once}\td{2}\td{4735}\td{4101 3842}\td{3972}\td{3842 - 4101}\td{-28.9\%}\td{yes}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{reachability}\td{s1 + evc + once}\td{2}\td{5516}\td{4385 4386}\td{4386}\td{4385 - 4386}\td{-21.5\%}\td{yes}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{Cedar slice}\td{v0}\td{7}\td{3153}\td{1950 1881 1852 1862 1864 1986 1838}\td{1890}\td{1838 - 1986}\td{-}\td{-}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{Cedar slice}\td{v0 + evc}\td{2}\td{3602}\td{2047 2032}\td{2040}\td{2032 - 2047}\td{+7.9\%}\td{yes}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{Cedar slice}\td{v0 + once}\td{7}\td{3157}\td{1862 1826 1887 1844 2045 1762 1834}\td{1866}\td{1762 - 2045}\td{-1.3\%}\td{no}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{Cedar slice}\td{v0 + evc + once}\td{5}\td{3557}\td{1857 1834 1839 1935 1926}\td{1878}\td{1834 - 1935}\td{-0.6\%}\td{no}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{Cedar slice}\td{s1}\td{4}\td{3136}\td{2079 1970 1866 1998}\td{1978}\td{1866 - 2079}\td{-}\td{-}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{Cedar slice}\td{s1 + once}\td{2}\td{3128}\td{1841 1953}\td{1897}\td{1841 - 1953}\td{-4.1\%}\td{no}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{Cedar slice}\td{s1 + evc + once}\td{2}\td{3221}\td{2075 1915}\td{1995}\td{1915 - 2075}\td{+0.8\%}\td{no}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{Init}\td{v0}\td{3}\td{6812}\td{5402 5425 5560}\td{5462}\td{5402 - 5560}\td{-}\td{-}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{Init}\td{v0 + once}\td{1}\td{6631}\td{5406}\td{5406}\td{5406 - 5406}\td{-1.0\%}\td{no}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{Init}\td{v0 + evc + once}\td{2}\td{6910}\td{5202 5559}\td{5380}\td{5202 - 5559}\td{-1.5\%}\td{no}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{Init}\td{s1}\td{3}\td{6119}\td{5430 5434 5073}\td{5312}\td{5073 - 5434}\td{-}\td{-}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{Init}\td{s1 + once}\td{1}\td{6456}\td{4997}\td{4997}\td{4997 - 4997}\td{-5.9\%}\td{yes}\td{ACCEPT}}
\tr{\td{Init}\td{s1 + evc + once}\td{2}\td{6376}\td{5008 5017}\td{5012}\td{5008 - 5017}\td{-5.6\%}\td{yes}\td{ACCEPT}}
}

\p{How to read it. A process is still warming up in its middle pass (5-15 \% slower than its last pass on the Cedar slice), so rows are compared on the LAST pass of each process. The processes of one row differ by up to 16 \% (Cedar slice, \code{\verb~|once~}) and the same row moved by up to 7 \% between two windows (Init, s1), so a row is called different from its base only when the two ranges do not overlap ("ranges disjoint"); with one or two processes per row that is thin, and it is all there is. The explanations below are readings, not measurements.}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Reachability: \code{\verb~|once~} alone -27 \% against v0 (5,687 -> 4,143 ms; cold first pass 6,816 -> 5,246 ms, -23 \%) and -29 \% against s1 (5,585 -> 3,972 ms).} Ranges disjoint in both. This is the corpus where 43 \% of the records were tabling records that nobody found again, in sessions of millions of records - where M1's profile has 39 \% of the process waiting for intern-table slots.}
\li{\strong{\code{\verb~|evc~} costs time wherever it can be told apart.} Alone on the Cedar slice: +7.9 \% (both processes above all seven v0 processes). In front of \code{\verb~|once~} on reachability: 4,422 against 4,143 ms under v0 and 4,386 against 3,972 ms under s1 (+6.7 \%, +10.4 \%; ranges disjoint from \code{\verb~|once~} alone both times). On the Cedar slice and on Init it is not distinguishable from \code{\verb~|once~} alone (Init under s1: 5,008 and 5,017 ms against 4,997 ms). It removes the second evaluations from the tick count and adds a key hash, a cache line and a store on EVERY evaluated node; in time the second evaluations were the cheaper of the two.}
\li{\strong{Cedar slice: no resolved effect of \code{\verb~|once~}.} -1.3 \% over seven processes each, ranges overlapping (the first window alone, two processes each, had -3.7 \%); under s1 -4.1 \%, ranges overlapping. The sessions there are small (1,195 records on average in v0), so the tables a tabling record goes into are small too.}
\li{\strong{Init: no resolved effect against v0} (\code{\verb~|once~} -1.0 \%, one process; \code{\verb~|evc + once~} -1.5 \%, ranges overlapping). \strong{Under s1 both \code{\verb~|once~} (4,997 ms, one process) and \code{\verb~|evc + once~} (5,008 / 5,017 ms) are below all three s1 processes (5,073 - 5,434 ms): about -6 \% against their mean.}}
\li{s1 itself (\code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~}) is not resolved against v0 on reachability (5,585 against 5,687 ms) and on Init (5,312 against 5,462 ms), and is slower on the Cedar slice in the mean (1,978 against 1,890 ms, ranges overlapping). This is one worker on the JVM and says nothing about the reasons for that default.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{5.5 Go / no-go}

\p{"Go" means: worth handing to the owner as a staging switch, on the evidence of ONE worker on the JVM launcher.}

\table{
\tr{\th{Scheme}\th{Verdict}\th{Why (census / prototype)}}
\tr{\td{(a) one bit "fresh and unpublished" on the newest record, in-place extension / pruning}\td{\strong{NO-GO}}\td{the cases are 1.9-7.2 \% of the records (spines) and 0.4-3.4 \% of the new frames; in v0 the source is always held by a memo word or an environment (E0 in 0.0 \% of the cases); a rewrite saves bytes, not a probe (argued, not built)}}
\tr{\td{(b1) region rollback per judgment (mark / release of records and runs)}\td{\strong{NO-GO as a speed-up}, v2 if a memory wall is measured}\td{releasing costs one probe per record, as making did; it needs an undo log at every memo store and a flush of every id-keyed cache; what it would release is what (e1) never makes (not built)}}
\tr{\td{(b3) non-interned NEU / closures / frames (\code{\verb~|REF_EPH~})}\td{\strong{not prototyped: v2 experiment}, yardstick reachability}\td{it is where the remaining volume is (with \code{\verb~|evc + once~} NEU are 59 \% and LAM closures 23 \% of the records on reachability, 3.5 \% and 1.3 \% found again), but it gives up I-ID and every identity-keyed memo on those values; needs its own soundness review}}
\tr{\td{(c) saturating 2-bit counts in the header}\td{\strong{NO-GO}}\td{no free header bits; a write on every store; counts never fall and do not see Java locals; no constructor has count-0 operands to specialise on (NEU: 0.0 \%)}}
\tr{\td{(d) builders}\td{\strong{already the design}; nothing new}\td{spines, frames and environments are built once (1 PUSH copy in 162 M); the one intermediate left (the prefix of an extended application) is 2-7 \% of the records and is a memoised or bound value}}
\tr{\td{(e1) \code{\verb~|once~}: one bit of visit count per tabling KEY, table at the second evaluation}\td{\strong{GO} (patch \code{\verb~|0001~}, owner M2), as a staging switch}\td{records -18 \% / -30 \% / -41 \% (Cedar slice / Init / reachability), run words -13 \% / -33 \% / -43 \%, peak RSS of the JVM on reachability 3,052 -> 1,533 MiB, for +5.8 \% / +5.4 \% / +0.7 \% ticks. Warm check time, one worker, JVM: \strong{reachability -27 \% against v0 and -29 \% against s1} (ranges disjoint); Init under s1 about -6 \% (one process, below all three s1 processes); Cedar slice and Init against v0: no resolved change (-1.3 \%, -1.0 \%). Verdicts identical, differential clean}}
\tr{\td{(e2) \code{\verb~|evc~}: ephemeral EVAL memo with the key inline}\td{\strong{NO-GO as built}}\td{in counters it does what it was designed for (alone: every counter identical to v0; with \code{\verb~|once~}: ticks +1.0 \% / +0.6 \% / +0.2 \% instead of +5.8 \% / +5.4 \% / +0.7 \%; under s1 the pair has 2-11 \% fewer ticks than s1) and in time it is never ahead of \code{\verb~|once~} alone: alone +7.9 \% on the Cedar slice; in front of \code{\verb~|once~} 6.7 \% (v0) and 10.4 \% (s1) slower than \code{\verb~|once~} alone on reachability; indistinguishable from it on the Cedar slice and on Init. Ticks are not time}}
\tr{\td{(e3) \code{\verb~|prof~}: two-bit counter per term node}\td{\strong{NO-GO}}\td{measured only behind \code{\verb~|evc~}, where it has nothing left to fix (+0.8 \% against +1.0 \% ticks, at the price of 1.6 points of records)}}
}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{6. Patches and owners}

\p{\code{\verb~|work/prof/X1/patches/~} (\code{\verb~|README.md~} there has the same table and the to-do list for the owners):}

\table{
\tr{\th{Patch}\th{File}\th{Owner (\code{\verb~|scripts/machine-sandbox.sh owner src/main/java/rlvm/machine/Eval.java~})}\th{Status}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|0001-eval-visit-filter.main-1653Z.patch~}}\td{\src{rlvm-machine/src/main/java/rlvm/machine/Eval.java}}\td{\strong{M2}}\td{\strong{the GO item}: \code{\verb~|once~} alone, 117 added lines, against the main tree as copied at 16:53:19Z (M2 published \code{\verb~|Eval.java~} three times after my base: 15:26Z, 15:34Z, 16:48Z). Checked on exactly this tree: section 5.3, item 4}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|full-prototype-evc-once-prof.base-1509Z.patch~}}\td{the same file}\td{\strong{M2}}\td{everything that was measured (\code{\verb~|once~}, \code{\verb~|evc~}, \code{\verb~|prof~}; 298 added lines) against the main tree of 15:09:21Z: the build the numbers of this report come from. \code{\verb~|evc~} and \code{\verb~|prof~} are no-go (5.5); kept for the record}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|full-prototype-evc-once-prof.main-1612Z.patch~}}\td{the same file}\td{\strong{M2}}\td{the same on the main tree of 16:12:20Z; counter-identical to the measured build and differential clean (section 5.3); it no longer applies after 16:48Z}}
}

\p{One file, one owner. What the GO patch deliberately does not touch, and who would:}

\ul{
\li{\strong{M6} (\code{\verb~|Op.java~}, \code{\verb~|Debug.parseSwitches~}, \code{\verb~|MachineProvider~}, \code{\verb~|SWITCHES.md~}, \code{\verb~|MachineEngine~}): a staging-switch name for bit 128 (proposal \code{\verb~|once~}), off in strict mode like every memo decision beyond the generic tier; the counters \code{\verb~|Eval.Ext.onceFirst~}, \code{\verb~|onceSeen~} into the statistics file.}
\li{\strong{M2} (\code{\verb~|Eval.java~}): (1) \code{\verb~|Eval.Ext.bytes()~} must count the filter and its log (\code{\verb~|8 * once.length + 4 * onceN~} bytes) so that the session cap sees them; (2) the log costs 4 bytes per first-visit key: a second filter level would replace it; (3) the filter's pass over the kept bindings and the one of M1's combined \code{\verb~|Values.suspRecordAt~} (in \code{\verb~|table~} since 16:48Z) could be shared; (4) INFER's own tabling records (\code{\verb~|SUSP~} by other callers: 9-18 \% of the records on the INFER-driven corpora, 30-61 \% never found again) are the same kind of key and are M5's: not tried.}
\li{\strong{M1} (\code{\verb~|Runs~}, \code{\verb~|Values~}): nothing to change. Two notes from the census: frames are 75 \% HOLE on the Cedar slice and 54 \% on con-leche (C4); and with the filter on, the PRUNE probes that remain are those of closures and delayed arguments (section 5.2).}
\li{\strong{M8}: the switch changes ticks, memo contents and the representation of values up to PEEK, like \code{\verb~|gated~}: tier and convention equivalence compare with the switch on both sides.}
}

\p{The census tooling is not a patch: \code{\verb~|work/prof/X1/census/~} (\code{\verb~|instrument.py~} applies 54 exact-match hooks - 58 on the prototype's tree - and \code{\verb~|Shadow.java~} to a COPY of the module; \code{\verb~|report.py~} / \code{\verb~|summary.py~} / \code{\verb~|probes.py~} make the tables). It can be re-run on any later tree; a hook that no longer matches fails loudly.}
}

\subtree{
\title{7. Not established}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Parallel workers.} Every number here is one worker. The owner's metric is warm wall clock with 8 workers; the filter is a per-worker array, so nothing is shared, and the saving on reachability is cache traffic that 8 workers compete for - which may make it larger or smaller; not measured.}
\li{\strong{The native image.} All runs are the JVM launcher (C2). The integration log has the native image at 0.5-0.9x the CPU time of the JVM launcher on Init, Std and the Cedar slice; the relative gain there is not known.}
\li{\strong{Steady state, and small effects.} A process checked the export 2 or 3 times; the last pass is the warmest one measured, not a proven steady state. Rows have one to seven processes; on the Cedar slice and on Init against v0 the effect of \code{\verb~|once~} is inside the spread (section 5.4), so "no resolved change" is not "no change".}
\li{\strong{Timing on the newest tree.} Every timing is the build of 15:09Z. On the main tree as copied at 16:53Z (which runs \code{\verb~|gated,expect,warm~} with a 1 MiB cap by default) only counters were taken: Cedar slice +5.3 \% ticks / -15.6 \% records, reachability +0.4 \% / -37.6 \%.}
\li{\strong{The large corpora} (mathlib, cslib, navier-stokes-euler, full cedar): not run. Std and con-leche: counters of \code{\verb~|once~} only, no timing.}
\li{\strong{M8's full gate with the switch} (tier and convention equivalence, mutants, audits, the 230 tests through the driver): not run. The differential run over all 230 tests with \code{\verb~|evc + once~} was stopped by me after 15 minutes in the heavy perf files (at least 200 of the 230 files were done; no report was written, so it is no evidence).}
\li{\strong{Why exactly \code{\verb~|evc~} costs 7-10 \%.} The prototype computes the node mask and the key hash up to three times per evaluated node and writes a cell per evaluation; a leaner form may pay, but nothing here shows that it would.}
\li{\strong{(b3), non-interned NEU / closures}: only its census bound is known (section 4); no prototype.}
\li{\strong{Reads through Java locals} are invisible to the census: "dead at return" is an upper bound (section 1).}
}
}
